  "notes": "CONJUGATION: Godan verb. メモる → メモった (past) → メモって (te-form) → メモらない (negative). The っ in メモった is a common source of confusion — it follows godan conjugation, not ichidan.\n\nFormed from メモ (memo, from English) + る. This pattern of creating verbs from loanwords by adding る is productive in casual Japanese. Similar examples:\n- コピる — to copy\n- サボる — to skip/slack off (from サボタージュ)\n- ググる — to google\n- ミスる — to make a mistake\n\nCasual/informal. In formal contexts, use メモを{取|と}る or {書|か}き{留|と}める instead.",
